# CORRECTION (2026-05-29): RULE-IDEA-SERVER-DATA-001 was MISFIRED in the original run.
# This is a pure-KMP app that CONSUMES an external REST API (Open Bank Project) and owns
# NO backend / NO database. Two independent gates require this rule to be SKIPPED:
#   1. requires_capability: has_api — ZERO screens declare `has_api` (all declare only
#      `capabilities: [has_ui]`). The original run inferred has_api from the presence of
#      api.yaml siblings, which violates the capability-declaration contract.
#   2. PROJECT_CONFIG.yaml has no `server.backends` block → whole-rule skip precondition
#      (RULE-IDEA-SERVER-DATA-001 Enforcement line 145 / Evaluation line 168).
# server/tables/ (owned DB schema) and apis↔flows 1:1 do NOT apply to an external-API
# consumer. The OBP contracts under server/apis/ + api_manifest.yaml remain valid as
# CLIENT contracts for Ktorfit codegen — they are not owned-backend artifacts.

